/**
 * @defgroup TestGeo TestGeo — Test and Tutorial Geometry Module
 * @ingroup StarVMCGeometry
 * @brief Minimal AGML geometry module for development, testing, and tutorial purposes.
 *
 * The `TestGeo` directory contains a single AGML module (`TestGeo1`) that
 * demonstrates advanced placement features of the AGML XML language.  It has
 * no correspondence to a real STAR detector and carries no sensitive volumes.
 *
 * @par Contents
 * `TestGeo1.xml` defines module `TestGeo1` with the following volume hierarchy:
 *
 * @code
 * Cave
 * └── MAIN  [Box 200×200×200 cm, Air]         — master volume
 *     └── TUBD  [Division along Y, 5 slices]  — replicated division
 *         └── TUBP  [Box dz=50 cm, Air]        — division cell
 *             └── TUBE  [Tube, Iron, parameterized=true]
 *                        — 11 placements with rmax = 1..6..1 cm
 * @endcode
 *
 * @par Features demonstrated
 * - **Parameterized shapes**: the `TUBE` volume has `rmin`, `rmax`, and `dz`
 *   set to zero in the volume definition and overridden individually at each
 *   `<Placement>` call, exercising the AGML parameterized-placement mechanism.
 * - **Volume division**: `TUBD` uses `<Shape type="Division" iaxis="2"
 *   ndiv="5">` to divide the mother along the Y-axis into five equal slices
 *   without explicit coordinate arithmetic.
 *
 * @par Intended use cases
 * - Validating the AGML parameterized-placement code path.
 * - Validating AGML volume division.
 * - Minimal self-contained example for learning the AGML XML language.
 * - Standalone regression test that requires no real detector configuration.
 *
 * @note No `TestGeoConfig.xml` exists; this module is loaded directly by name.
 * @note No hit instrumentation is defined; this module produces no simulation hits.
 *
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @var TestGeo1
 * @brief Parameterized tube + division test module.
 * Defined in TestGeo1.xml.  Author: JCW.
 */

/**
 * @}
 */
